\tag{frap}
\title{From incidence to moves}

\p{Faces and incidence define an abstract polytope without choosing
lengths or an embedding \citet{Section 2}{schulte2017regular}.
Regularity supplies shape symmetries; the Rubik construction applies
facet rotations locally to incidence positions
\citet{Definitions 5--6}{marchetti2025rubik}. The sections below build
this action and calculate tetrahedron and cube examples.}

\transclude{frap-0008}
